scope: |
  MEASURED on origin/main 2026-08-10: 39 LEDGER rows against 7 claim files. Every one of the 32
  extras has a release-claim commit, so none is a lost claim -- they are rows that outlived their
  work. The count has sat near 37 for days, moving +-1 per claim/release, so this is a backlog that
  never drains, not a spike.

  IT BLOCKS NOBODY, and that is why it survived: the pre-push overlap guard enumerates
  .work/active/*.claim (pre-push:189) and never reads a row. The damage is to a READER. On this day
  an agent (me) grepped the ledger for scripts/smoke-ci.ssc, found two rows, concluded the file was
  held and asked its "holder" to make a change -- both rows were dead. Nothing failed; work was
  handed away on a stale file.

  THE OTHER DIRECTION has never been checked either and is worse: board walks the ledger's slugs and
  skips any without a claim file, so a claim whose row is MISSING is invisible on the board.

  FIX, and the project already chose it once: the row is a verbatim copy of claim fields
  (slug<-filename, agent, started, items, paths), so generate it rather than maintain it -- the same
  reasoning scripts/board's header sets out for the SPRINT table, ending "the fix is not a better
  gate, it is not keeping the second copy". scripts/coord-ledger --write/--check/--self-test, the
  check wired into smoke beside board-generated.
next: verify smoke green with the new check, then land
